{
  "assessment": "Extent of change:\n\nThe diff introduces a fresh implementation of `safeGet` that splits the dot-separated path and iteratively accesses object properties. It correctly preserves genuinely-present falsy values by checking strict equality against `undefined`. However, it lacks any guards to prevent property access on intermediate null or undefined values, directly contradicting the requirement for graceful handling along the traversal.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'b')`",
      "at": "Intermediate property is null/undefined during traversal",
      "call": "`node --input-type=module -e 'import(\"./solution.mjs\").then(m => m.safeGet({a:null}, \"a.b\", \"default\"))'`",
      "defect": "While iterating over the path parts, the code blindly accesses `current[part]`. When an intermediate value is explicitly `null` or `undefined`, this triggers a TypeError. The task requires these to be handled gracefully (by returning the default).",
      "expected": "\"default\" (or undefined) without throwing"
    }
  ]
}
